{{ 'ka-voice-of-bride.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Voice of the Bride — conditionally hidden until real review data is present.

  Data source (added 2026-08-29, pending task #3 -- live Google Reviews sync):
  Suraj decided against a third-party embed widget (Elfsight/EmbedSocial/etc.)
  and is instead getting Owner-level Google Business Profile API access
  directly, so this section reads from a single JSON metafield instead --
  `shop.metafields.custom.google_reviews` (definition created 2026-08-29,
  gid://shopify/MetafieldDefinition/292565483810). That metafield is written
  by a droplet cron job (scripts/google-reviews-sync/, same pattern as the
  Petty Cash bot on the stocktradingbot droplet) once Suraj's Google API
  access is approved -- see that script for the sync flow. Until then the
  metafield is empty and this section falls back to the pre-existing
  editor-block behaviour untouched below.

  Expected JSON shape of shop.metafields.custom.google_reviews.value:
    {
      "rating_number": "4.9",
      "rating_count": 52,
      "rating_label": "4.9 · 52 Google Reviews",
      "google_url": "https://g.page/r/xxxxxxxxxxxx",
      "reviews": [
        { "quote": "...", "reviewer_name": "Priya S.", "occasion": "", "rating": 5 },
        { "quote": "...", "reviewer_name": "Anika R.", "occasion": "", "rating": 4 }
      ],
      "synced_at": "2026-08-29T00:00:00Z"
    }

  The section renders only when section.settings.show_section is true AND
  there is actual content to show -- either synced metafield data (preferred)
  or at least one editor block with non-empty quote text (fallback, e.g. for
  manual curation before live sync is wired up). This prevents an empty or
  broken-looking section from ever going live by accident.
  Creative Director spec note: "Do not publish placeholder review content."
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign reviews_data = shop.metafields.custom.google_reviews.value

  assign synced_quote_count = 0
  for review in reviews_data.reviews
    if review.quote != blank
      assign synced_quote_count = synced_quote_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  assign has_synced_data = false
  if reviews_data != blank and synced_quote_count > 0 and reviews_data.rating_label != blank
    assign has_synced_data = true
  endif

  assign block_quote_count = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.quote != blank
      assign block_quote_count = block_quote_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
  assign has_editor_content = false
  if block_quote_count > 0
    assign has_editor_content = true
  endif

  assign has_content = false
  if has_synced_data or has_editor_content
    assign has_content = true
  endif

  if has_synced_data
    comment
      Synced values are UNTRUSTED text (public Google reviews, written by a
      cron job) and Liquid does not auto-escape output, so escape everything
      that comes from the metafield. The editor-setting fallbacks below are
      merchant-entered and left exactly as before.
    endcomment
    assign rating_number = reviews_data.rating_number | escape
    assign rating_label = reviews_data.rating_label | escape
    assign synced_google_url = reviews_data.google_url
    if synced_google_url != blank
      assign google_url = synced_google_url | escape
    else
      comment
        The sync's GOOGLE_REVIEW_URL env var may be unset/blank; never let
        the CTA render an empty href -- fall back to the editor setting.
      endcomment
      assign google_url = section.settings.google_url
    endif
  else
    assign rating_number = section.settings.rating_number
    assign rating_label = section.settings.rating_label
    assign google_url = section.settings.google_url
  endif
-%}

{% if section.settings.show_section and has_content %}
<section class="ka-voices" aria-label="What our brides say">
  <div class="ka-voices__inner">
    <div class="ka-voices__header reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-dark" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        <h2 class="ka-voices__title">{{ section.settings.title }}</h2>
      </div>
      {% if rating_number != blank %}
        <div class="ka-voices__rating-block">
          <span class="ka-voices__rating-number">{{ rating_number }}</span>
          <span class="ka-voices__rating-label">{{ rating_label }}</span>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      Extended from 3 to 5 entries (2026-09-11, Google review count
      64->67 update) to cover up to 5 editor-block review cards without
      indexing out of bounds -- reveal-delay-3/-4 already exist in
      ka-base.css (unused elsewhere in this file until now), so this
      needed no new CSS. The synced-data path now loops `limit: 6`
      (2026-09-21, fully automatic card selection: the sync picks up to
      MAX_REVIEWS=6 eligible 4-5 star reviews with text -- a full 3 x 2
      grid) and uses the same delay_classes (ka-base.css only defines
      reveal-delay-1..4, so the 5th and 6th cards both reuse -4). The
      grid layout for 6/5/4/3/2/1 cards is pure CSS quantity queries on
      the rendered cards (assets/ka-voice-of-bride.css), so fewer than 6
      cards never leaves an empty cell. Per Docs/google-reviews-sections-
      build-spec.md sec 1.4: on the SYNCED path the (blank) occasion slot
      is replaced by the real star rating of the review (each synced review
      carries a numeric `rating`), and quotes are cut at a word boundary
      after 40 words (truncatewords, then escape -- truncate first so the
      count is on raw text). The editor-block path is untouched: it keeps
      its occasion field and is never truncated.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% assign delay_classes = 'reveal, reveal reveal-delay-1, reveal reveal-delay-2, reveal reveal-delay-3, reveal reveal-delay-4, reveal reveal-delay-4' | split: ', ' %}
    {% if has_synced_data %}
      <div class="ka-voices__grid">
        {% for review in reviews_data.reviews limit: 6 %}
          {% if review.quote != blank %}
            <div class="ka-voice-card {{ delay_classes[forloop.index0] }}">
              <div class="ka-voice-card__quote-mark">&ldquo;</div>
              <p class="ka-voice-card__quote">{{ review.quote | truncatewords: 40, '…' | escape }}</p>
              <div class="ka-voice-card__meta">
                <span class="ka-voice-card__name">{{ review.reviewer_name | escape }}</span>
                {%- comment -%} plus: 0 coerces to a number (a non-numeric value can never reach the aria-label); round + at_most: 5 clamp it to at most 5, and r > 0 below means 1-5 {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign r = review.rating | plus: 0 | round | at_most: 5 -%}
                {%- if r > 0 -%}<span class="ka-voice-card__stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ r }} out of 5 stars">{% for i in (1..5) %}{% if i <= r %}&#9733;{% else %}&#9734;{% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% elsif section.blocks.size > 0 %}
      <div class="ka-voices__grid">
        {% for block in section.blocks %}
          {% if block.settings.quote != blank %}
            <div class="ka-voice-card {{ delay_classes[forloop.index0] }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="ka-voice-card__quote-mark">&ldquo;</div>
              <p class="ka-voice-card__quote">{{ block.settings.quote }}</p>
              <div class="ka-voice-card__meta">
                <span class="ka-voice-card__name">{{ block.settings.reviewer_name }}</span>
                <span class="ka-voice-card__occasion">{{ block.settings.occasion }}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    {%- if google_url != blank -%}
    <div class="ka-voices__cta reveal reveal-delay-3">
      <a href="{{ google_url }}" class="btn-outline-rose" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        {{ section.settings.google_cta_label }}
      </a>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Voice of the Bride",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Prefers live-synced data from the custom.google_reviews Shop metafield (written automatically by the droplet Google Reviews sync job) when present. The rating, review URL, and review cards below are only a manual fallback used before that sync is active."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_section",
      "label": "Show this section",
      "default": false,
      "info": "IMPORTANT: Only enable once real review data exists, either synced automatically or entered manually below. Do not publish with placeholder content."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow",          "label": "Eyebrow",         "default": "What Brides Say" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title",             "label": "Section title",   "default": "The words of\nour brides." },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Rating block (manual fallback)"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "rating_number", "label": "Rating (e.g. 4.9 or ★★★★★)",    "info": "Leave blank to hide the rating block. Ignored once live sync data exists." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "rating_label",  "label": "Rating label (e.g. 4.9 · 52 Google Reviews)" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "CTA"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "google_cta_label", "label": "Google reviews CTA label", "default": "Read all reviews on Google" },
    { "type": "url",  "id": "google_url",        "label": "Google Maps review URL (manual fallback)",  "info": "Obtain from your Google Business Profile. Ignored once live sync data exists." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "review",
      "name": "Review",
      "limit": 6,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "quote",
          "label": "Review quote (verbatim from Google)",
          "info": "Must be the exact text from the reviewer's Google review. Do not paraphrase."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "reviewer_name", "label": "Reviewer first name and initial (e.g. Priya S.)" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "occasion",       "label": "Occasion and year (e.g. Bridal, 2024)" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Voice of the Bride" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
